factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 4 problems
  The article says the farmers protested to get water released from Bhavanisagar dam for the first crop irrigation area's 20-day special wetting; the draft's reel_script says they demanded opening the Bhavanisagar dam water channel in general, which is a slightly different claim but not clearly wrong.
  The reel_script says the collector explained the rotation-based water release 'will be recommended' and that the agriculture department data would be used; the article says the collector stated that the Kilbhavani dry irrigation water release would be recommended from Dec 15 to Apr 15, which matches, but the draft omits that the request for special wetting could not be recommended was said after the rotation statement in the article, so ordering is loosely reversed only in the draft's 'ஆனால்' framing, which is acceptable.
  The reel_script states the collector 'அணுகி பேசுமாறும்' pointed farmers to district minister Sengottaiyan, but the draft's reel_script says 'மாவட்ட அமைச்சர் செங்கோட்டையனை அணுகி பேசுமாறும் விவசாயிகளுக்கு அறிவுறுத்தினார்' which is consistent; however the slides_spec 'கலெக்டர் கூறியது' third line is cut off mid-sentence ('விவசாயிகளுக்கு') with no clear meaning, making it an incomplete Tamil sentence.
  The reel_script states the collector said the Kodiveri and Kalingarayan irrigation water being released out of turn 'அதிகாரிகளிடம் விசாரிக்கப்படும்' — this is supported, but the article says it is about whether such release should be stopped, which the draft omits; the important point that the minister should also be approached on this is missing from the reel_script.
